# Gallery Wall

Physical gallery-wall layout tool: arrange frames around a centerpiece for real-world hanging.

## Repository layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `layout/` | **Standalone Go module** (`github.com/yashdalfthegray/gallery-wall/layout`, v1.0.0). Core placement algorithm — publishable without the rest of the repo. |
| `wasm/` | Go WASM bridge exposing `goLayout(json)` to the browser |
| `web/` | TypeScript + Vite + Web Awesome static app; runs layout locally via WASM |
| `cmd/gallery-svg/` | Dev helper: result JSON → SVG diagram (not part of the library) |
| `scripts/build-wasm.sh` | Builds `web/public/layout.wasm` + copies `wasm_exec.js` |
| `docs/DESIGN.md` | Original algorithm spec (some v1 scope notes are stale — see rules below) |
| `layout/ALGORITHM.md` | Implementation walkthrough aligned with current code |
| `layout/README.md` | Library install/usage for external Go consumers |

**Do not use Python** for the core algorithm.

## Stack (current)

| Layer | Tech | Status |
|-------|------|--------|
| Core algorithm | Go `layout/` nested module | **Complete** (v1.0.0) |
| Browser runtime | Go WASM (`wasm/`) | **Complete** |
| Frontend | TypeScript, Vite, Web Awesome | **Complete** (local-only static app) |
| HTTP API | Go server wrapping `layout` | Not started |

## Module wiring

- Root `go.mod` + `go.work` wire the monorepo; `replace` points at `./layout`.
- External consumers: `go get github.com/yashdalfthegray/gallery-wall/layout@v1.0.0` (tag `layout/v1.0.0`).
- From repo root: `go test ./layout/...`. From `layout/`: `go test .`.

## Agent workflow

1. Read file-specific rules when touching `layout/`, `web/`, or `wasm/` (see `.cursor/rules/`).
2. Prefer minimal, focused diffs; match existing conventions in each area.
3. Run relevant tests (`go test ./layout/...`, `npm run build` in `web/` when UI changes).
4. Keep GitHub Actions green: PR workflow runs layout tests + web format/build; `main` deploys Pages.
5. **Do not commit** unless the user asks.

## Design decisions (locked)

- **Input:** `{ id, height, width, shape, centerpiece }` + global `gap`. Optional `wallWidth` / `wallHeight` constrain the cluster to a rectangle centered on the anchor.
- **Dimensions are source of truth;** shape is geometry/rendering hint only (no shape/dimension validation).
- **Anchor:** Centerpiece center at `(0, 0)`. Output `centerX`/`centerY`, derived top-left `x`/`y`, hanging helpers (`offsetFromAnchor`, `direction`, `adjacentIds`).
- **Layout:** Organic connected **blob** — no floaters. Every non-centerpiece frame must be adjacent to the cluster.
- **Silhouette:** Mostly round, **wider than tall** (target aspect ~1.3–1.6).
- **Candidates:** 1-unit step size along attachment edges.

Algorithm spec: `docs/DESIGN.md` · Implementation detail: `layout/ALGORITHM.md`.

## Code conventions

- Go: table-driven tests; golden fixtures in `layout/testdata/`. Public entry: `layout.Layout(params Params) (Result, error)`.
- Web: no framework beyond Web Awesome components; custom Form/JSON tabs (do not use `wa-tab-group` — inactive panels need `[hidden]`, not `[active]`).
- WASM artifacts live in `web/public/` and are gitignored; rebuilt via `scripts/build-wasm.sh`.
